#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:25
#. Diagram label
msgid "Administrator"
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:114
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "After the release is live, every published identifier resolves to the file it names."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:63
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Asked AT SEED TIME, because the tree has moved since `8 · Rehearse`. A seed is a snapshot with no history, so every open PR over the layer when it is taken is orphaned into the monorepo. Computed by decisions/seed-readiness-gate.dmn (hit policy FIRST) from `seed:ready --layer <name>`: an open `heavy-mover` PR over the layer or the next one, any open PR on the next layer, more than five over the layer, any that moves a file in it, a red sibling-layout rehearsal, or a direct dependent that discovery cannot find among sibling clones answers `not yet`. A criterion that could not be decided answers `unknown` and stops; it never hides a finding already certain, which is why the `not yet` rows come first. The rehearsal runs only on request (`--rehearse`, owner ruling 2026-10-02), so without it the answer is never `settled`."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:30
#. Diagram label
msgid "Authoring agent"
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:142
#. Diagram label
msgid "Beans"
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:125
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Both repositories seeded, the parent consumes them, and the first release dereferences."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:31
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Briefs, measures the signals, runs declare-detangle-isolate, reports what would move, seeds the repositories once they exist, and adopts each later release. Verification is always by re-running a gate, never by a change looking right."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:35
#. Diagram label
msgid "Build pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:54
#. Diagram label
