#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:36
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs the checks that decide the gateways: the tools' import closure and the content's lack of code, node identifiers against file paths, the standalone rehearsal, and dereferencing after release. A gate that cannot tell stops the process; it never reads as clean."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:80
#. Diagram label
msgid "Seed both repositories"
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Seed main, then bring the content and the tools in as reviewed pull requests with their history, so neither repository's first commit is unreviewable."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:137
#. Diagram label
msgid "settled"
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:103
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tag each repository, publish /v<major>/. From here the two are versioned independently; a tools release lists the content majors it supports."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The owner creates the content and tools repositories and their Pages. Nothing is committed to them before this."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:92
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The parent pins the pair (a commit while staging, a version once released) — a code dependency as a `source.remote` instance in its root `index.config.json` (remote-mount skill), never a submodule — repoints its imports, and keeps its own copy until it is green with the dependency declared."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:26
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The person's decisions: whether to separate at all, authorising the extraction, creating the repositories, and the cutover that retires the parent's copy. An agent reports and waits at each; none of them may be relaxed by a package."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The platform-side stages: the graph's identity (version, iriBase, nodeSchemas), moving harness output about it into the host, splitting the content from its tools, and making the parent consume the pair additively."
msgstr ""

